          "text": "{\"regions\":{\"r2\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"compounds having \u092d\u094b\u0917 for their latter member take \u0916 ( \u0908\u0928 )\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"in the sense of \u2018\u0924\u0938\u094d\u092e\u0948 \u0939\u093f\u0924\u092e\u094d\u2019 as \u092a\u093f\u0924\u0943\u092d\u094b\u0917\u0940\u0928 &c.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The Sanskrit suffix and example are not fully clear.\"},\"r3\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 72 \u0938\u094d\u0935\u0930\u094d\u0917\u0917\u094d\u0930\u093e\u092e\u0915\u0941\u091f\u0940\u2014The comparison of heaven to a village hut\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"shows the contempt with which a Ved\u00e1ntin, longing for Moksha,\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"treats the pleasures of heaven. \u0935\u093f\u092d\u094d\u0930\u092e\u2014Sport. \u092d\u0935\u092c\u0928\u094d\u0927\u0926\u0941\u0903\u0916\u0930\u091a\u0928\u093e\u2014\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"R\u00e0marshi explains \u0930\u091a\u0928\u093e by \u092a\u094d\u0930\u093e\u092a\u094d\u0924\u093f Mr. Telang takes it to mean\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"\u2018expanse\u2019, \u2018large extent,\u2019 but without any apparent authority.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"The meaning which naturally suggests itself from the primary\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"meaning \u2018arrangement\u2019 of the word, is \u2018predestination, prearrang-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"ing for future births.\u2019 \u0938\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0924\u094d\u092e\u093e\u0928\u0928\u094d\u0926 &c.\u2014\u0915\u0932\u0928\u0902 the compassing or\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"effecting of &c. R\u00e0marshi explains\u2014\u0938\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0924\u094d\u092e\u093e\u0928\u0928\u094d\u0926 \u090f\u0935 \u092a\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0928\u0928\u094d\u0926 \u090f\u0915\u0902\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":10,\"text\":\"\u092a\u0926\u0902 \u0935\u0938\u094d\u0924\u0941 \u0924\u0924\u094d\u0930 \u092a\u094d\u0930\u0935\u0947\u0936\u0915\u0932\u0928\u092e\u0928\u0941\u092d\u0935\u0927\u093e\u0930\u0923\u092e\u094d \u0964 \u0935\u0923\u093f\u0917\u094d\u0935\u0943\u0924\u094d\u0924\u092f\u0903\u2014mercenary doings.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":11,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Some Sanskrit and text at the damaged right edge are difficult to read.\"},\"r4\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 73 \u092f\u0926\u093e\u2014since, when. \u0927\u0930\u0923\u093f\u0927\u0930\u092a\u093e\u0926\u0948\u0903\u2014by the feet ( the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"hills at the foot ) of mountains; the mountains are said to\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"uphold the earth and have a number of synonymous words to\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"denote them from this circumstance, such as \u092e\u0939\u0940\u0927\u094d\u0930, \u092d\u0942\u092d\u0943\u0924\u094d &c.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"R\u00e1marshi gives as optional meaning \u2018\u0936\u0947\u0937\u2019. The word \u092a\u093e\u0926 presents\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"some difficulty in the way of accepting either sense, as the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"serpent S'esha has no feet, as also mountains. The adjacent hills\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"of mountains are, however, regarded as their feet and the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"mountains are described as supporting the earth with their feet.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":10,\"text\":\"So we may accept the meaning \u2018mountains\u2019 and reject \u2018S'esha\u2019.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":11,\"text\":\"The fig. is \u0915\u093e\u0935\u094d\u092f\u093e\u0930\u094d\u0925\u093e\u092a\u0924\u094d\u0924\u093f\u0903.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Some Sanskrit characters and punctuation at the right edge are unclear.\"},\"r5\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 74. \u0938\u0902\u0915\u0941\u091a\u093f\u0924\u0902\u2014Shrunken, shrivelled; \u0906\u0926\u094d\u0930\u093f\u092f\u0924\u0947\u2014fr. \u0926\u0943 A. 6\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"cl; \u0928 \u0936\u0941\u0936\u094d\u0930\u0942\u0937\u0924\u0947 does not serve, or attend to. \u0905\u092e\u093f\u0924\u094d\u0930\u093e\u092f\u0924\u0947\u2014\u0905\u092e\u093f\u0924\u094d\u0930 \u0907\u0935\u093e\u091a-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\u0930\u0924\u093f; denom. verb. Cf. Pt. IV. 75.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The Sanskrit at the right edge of line 2 is partly obscured.\"},\"r6\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 75. \u091c\u0930\u093e\u092a\u0930\u093f\u092d\u0935\u2014the injury or ravages done by old age.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"Cf. \u0935\u094d\u092f\u093e\u0918\u094d\u0930\u0940\u0935 &c. supra sl. 39. The reading \u0924\u0926\u093e \u092a\u0941\u092e\u093e\u0902\u0938\u092e\u094d is easier.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"We need not in this case supply \u092a\u0941\u0902\u0938. fr. \u092a\u0941\u0902\u0938\u093e\u0902 as object to \u092a\u0930\u093f\u0939-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"\u0930\u094d\u092f. \u0906\u0930\u094b\u092a\u093f\u0924\u2014Mr. Telang says that this refers to the bit of\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"bone suspended over a Ch\u00e2nd\u00e1lak\u00fbpa ( to distinguish it from\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"wells used by the higher classes. )\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Some Sanskrit words, particularly the split word in lines 3\u20134, are unclear.\"},\"r7\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 76. \u0938\u094d\u0935\u0938\u094d\u0925\u2014at ease, lit. in its natural condition i. e. not\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"enfeebled by diseases &c. \u0905\u0930\u0941\u091c\u0902\u2014free from disease; as this\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null},\"r1\":{\"type\":\"page_number\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"( 71 )\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null}},\"units\":[{\"id\":\"u1\",\"type\":\"notes\",\"number\":null,\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"u2\",\"u3\",\"u4\",\"u5\",\"u6\",\"u7\"]},{\"id\":\"u2\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":null,\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r2\"]},{\"id\":\"u3\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"72\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r3\"]},{\"id\":\"u4\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"73\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r4\"]},{\"id\":\"u5\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"74\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r5\"]},{\"id\":\"u6\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"75\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r6\"]},{\"id\":\"u7\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"76\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"r7\"]}],\"flows\":[{\"flow\":\"main\",\"units\":[\"u1\"]}],\"relations\":[]}"
        }
